    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "The main reason is readability. The `withHits` decorator only takes a function as an argument but it's not the case with this one. It feels like with the list of parameters reads better, but we can change it I don't have a strong opinion.\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// with list of parameters\r\nwithLifecycle(search, container, () =>\r\n  instantsearch.widgets.configure({\r\n    hitsPerPage: 1\r\n  })\r\n);\r\n\r\n// with named parameters\r\nwithLifecycle({\r\n  search,\r\n  container,\r\n  fn(node) {\r\n    instantsearch.widgets.searchBox({\r\n      container: node\r\n    });\r\n  }\r\n});\r\n```\r\n",
